
# Python bytecode, written wherever this component's modules are imported from.
# These rules lived in the repository root's .gitignore and covered every
# component through one file; each component is its own repository now, so the
# rule travels with the thing it describes, which is what that file already says
# for every other build product.
*.py[cod]
__pycache__/

# setuptools' scratch, left beside a distribution's source whenever one is BUILT.
# Shipping either would also SHADOW the module for every later run here.
*/build/
*/*.egg-info/

# pymetta-host's package data is BUILT, not source: a patched SWI-Prolog home
# of about 1,200 files and the janus bridge vendored beside it, staged by
# tools/pymetta-host/run.sh in the superproject. assemble.sh copies the package
# sources elsewhere and builds there, so these should never appear here; they
# are ignored because an interrupted in-place build once left 2,404 of those
# files in the tree, 21 of them Python, and every Python tool in the gate
# walked into swiplserver and SWI's own protobuf examples.
pymetta-host/pymetta_host/swipl/
pymetta-host/pymetta_host/_vendor/

# `python -m build`'s output, beside a distribution's source for the same
# reason its scratch directory above is.
*/dist/
